            <ArticleTitle>Enteric-coated, pH-dependent peppermint oil capsules for the treatment of irritable bowel syndrome in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a randomized, double-blind controlled trial, 42 children with irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) were given pH-dependent, enteric-coated peppermint oil capsules or placebo. After 2 weeks, 75% of those receiving peppermint oil had reduced severity of pain associated with IBS. Peppermint oil may be used as a therapeutic agent during the symptomatic phase of IBS.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
